---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="nykma: nobody knows my app"
  description="An ad maker that runs in Claude Code. It has the idea, builds the ad in code and hands you MP4s with post copy."
  page="home"
>
  <h1 class="headline">
    <span class="line">nobody knows</span>
    <span class="line"
      ><span class="struck"
        >my app.<svg viewBox="0 0 100 10" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"
          ><path d="M1 6.5 C 18 3.2, 34 8.4, 52 5.6 S 84 3.4, 99 6"></path></svg
        ></span
      ></span
    >
  </h1>
  <p class="lede">
    nykma is an ad maker that runs in Claude Code, on your machine. Ask for an ad and it has the idea, builds it in
    code and hands you MP4s with post copy, in English or Hebrew. It never posts anything, and spends nothing without
    your go-ahead.
  </p>
  <p class="lede">Tutorials are coming. For now: <a href="https://github.com/TomCohenDev/nykma">the code on GitHub</a>, free for personal use, and <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for companies.</p>
</Base>
